    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d744">

                <pb facs="0683" n="567" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg567"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 815.51/197.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Charles A. Conant
                        to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-02-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 11, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: I have examined the copies of the
                    proposed contracts between the bankers and the fiscal agent of the Government of
                    Honduras which are enclosed herewith,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d744-f1"/> with a
                    view to the changes made since my letter to the Department of February 6th
                    last.</p>
                <p>I do not find in the changes made any reason to modify the opinions expressed in
                    that letter. The changes appear to be of a nature to add to the protection
                    afforded to the Government of Honduras under the contract, and to give greater
                    clearness to certain minor provisions.</p>
                <p>Yours very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles A. Conant.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
